<article class="env-definition" id="01KD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KD">Definition <span data-tag="01KD">26.20.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ <em>satisfies the existence part of the valuative criterion</em> if given any commutative solid diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \ar[r] \ar@{-->}[ru] &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $A$ is a valuation ring with field of fractions $K$, the dotted arrow exists. We say $f$ <em>satisfies the uniqueness part of the valuative criterion</em> if there is at most one dotted arrow given any diagram as above (without requiring existence of course). </p>
</article>